  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering communities to respond to conflict protection risks and food insecuri</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian situation in the eastern provinces of the Democratic Republic of the Congo is worsening as violence perpetrated by armed groups and subsequent displacement continues to affect millions of vulnerable civilians. United Nations high Commission for Refugees (UNHCR), the United Nations Refugee Agency, expresses its deep concern about the difficult living conditions and human rights violations, including cases of sexual and gender -based violence, faced by more than 6.2 million internally displaced people in the country. So, to respond to the crises and structural conditions revealed in order to ensure the effectiveness of the humanitarian response in this part of the territory, Oxfam intends to deploy an intervention/action Protection, integrating  -Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WaSH) -Food, economic and livelihood security - as well as strengthening local governance through advocacy actions. The rationale is therefore to promote sustainable livelihoods, with a view to empowering women and reducing the vulnerability of young household heads, children and long -term internally displaced persons. It is an approach based on satisfying immediate needs, with a medium - and long -term vision, which consolidates the conditions for improving the resilience of households, communities and institutions at local level, and which will be applicable, within the framework of the present grant, to the social groups most exposed to the risks of Protection. Outcome 1: PROTECTION Oxfam, following its Protection vision for 2021 -2030 will aim at contributing to ensure that civilians caught up in conflicts and crises are safe and have their rights respected and fulfilled. Oxfam will support communities to develop and implement community -based initiatives to respond to and address protection threats. Crisis -affected households will also be supported to have access to timely and inclusive protection services and basic humanitarian needs. Joint activities and active participation in po</narrative>
  </description>
